{
    "word": "ragnarok",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "a04307bb-4a93-3c2a-9d27-c3ba7787e627",
                "word": "Ragnarok",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "964a4559-b20e-3d20-b82c-3d842cba4671",
                        "entry_id": "a04307bb-4a93-3c2a-9d27-c3ba7787e627",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A series of future events culminating in a battle, fought between the Æsir and einherjar on one side, and the forces of Surtr, Loki, and Loki's children on the other, in which all of creation is burned down and almost all life is extinguished."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Norse"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab747cb7-38c7-4ef0-b793-2133551db13a",
                                "sense_id": "964a4559-b20e-3d20-b82c-3d842cba4671",
                                "text": "Wilhelmina weeps, now and then, with her good Sonsfeld; hopes nevertheless there will be some dawn to this ragnarök, or general ‘twilight of the gods.’"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "119391f5-f4c7-4524-8ad6-6828b4683782",
                                "sense_id": "964a4559-b20e-3d20-b82c-3d842cba4671",
                                "text": "And all that is before them and the whole civilised world, would be long centuries of anarchy such as the world has not seen for ages—a true Ragnarok, a twilight of the very gods, an age such as the wise woman foretold in the old Voluspà."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e4d9612d-4f40-4bcc-af52-d2a3d0623260",
                                "sense_id": "964a4559-b20e-3d20-b82c-3d842cba4671",
                                "text": "But this heaven was not to last forever. Some day would come Ragnarok, or the Twilight of the Gods, when all creation would be destroyed, and all the Gods and men save Alfadur perish. Surtur, after killing the last of these Gods, would burn up the world."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "47eb9085-3058-4bfa-85da-3d41659e13f4",
                        "source_entry_id": "a04307bb-4a93-3c2a-9d27-c3ba7787e627",
                        "source_sense_id": "964a4559-b20e-3d20-b82c-3d842cba4671",
                        "source_sense_description": "the final battle in Norse mythology",
